      "writtenOn": "2024-08-03T22:21:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Aha, when you said `/system/framework/x86_64/$bootjar.vdex`, I thought of the product install path (`out/target/product/vsoc_x86_64/system/framework/x86_64/$bootjar.vdex`), so it looked wrong to me.\n\nI think the problem is that the expression `/system/framework/x86_64/$bootjar.vdex --\u003e /system/framework/$bootjar.vdex` is misleading. The former is a path relative to the dexpreopt dex_bootjars root, while the latter is a path relative to the product output root.\n\nI would omit the former to avoid the confusion, as it\u0027s not important anyway. I.e., I would change the comment to:\n\n```\n// Copy the vdex from the primary arch to the no-arch directory\n// e.g. /system/framework/$bootjar.vdex\n```",
